  "description": "Reid Let's Fold eBike | Folding Electric Bike\nCompact, practical and designed for everyday convenience – the Reid Let's Fold eBike combines smooth electric assistance with a folding design, making it ideal for city travel and leisure rides.\nIts lightweight 6061 alloy frame features internal cable routing and a 12.8Ah rack-mounted battery for a clean, streamlined look. The folding frame and compact 20-inch wheels make storage easier, particularly in homes with limited space.\nA 250W rear hub motor provides electric assistance to help tackle hills and everyday journeys. The LCD handlebar-mounted display keeps ride information clear and accessible, while an L-TWOO 7-speed trigger shifter paired with a Shimano rear derailleur offers practical gearing for urban streets and cycle paths.\nWide 20 x 2.0-inch tyres provide cushioning and grip across everyday riding surfaces, while front and rear alloy V-brakes deliver dependable stopping power. An alloy riser handlebar, ergonomic comfort grips and a city comfort saddle support a relaxed riding position. The alloy folding stem and resin folding pedals make the bike easier to store, while the 550mm alloy seatpost allows for riding position adjustments.\nWhether you're commuting, running errands or enjoying a leisurely ride, the Reid Let's Fold eBike offers a versatile and space-saving way to enjoy electric cycling.\nThe Reid Let's Fold eBike is ideal for:\n\nUrban commuters, with a compact design for navigating city streets and cycle paths\n\nRiders with limited storage space, thanks to its folding frame, stem and pedals\n\nEveryday journeys, with a 250W rear hub motor and 12.8Ah rack-mounted battery\n\nComfort-focused cyclists, with ergonomic grips, a city comfort saddle and alloy riser handlebars\n\nCity and leisure riding, with 20-inch wheels, 20 x 2.0-inch tyres and 7-speed gearing\n\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
